       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. An overdose raises the risk of severe lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals** (1,700 mg/day)\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**\n- Something else\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note saying you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
